.TH "GF-ADMIN-PROVISIONING-ADMIN-PROVISIONING-RELOAD-DASHBOARDS" "1" "Apr 2026" "" ""

.SH NAME
gf-admin-provisioning-admin-provisioning-reload-dashboards - Reloads dashboard provisioning configurations


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgf admin-provisioning admin-provisioning-reload-dashboards [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Reloads dashboard provisioning configurations

.PP
Reloads the provisioning config files for dashboards again. It won’t return until the new provisioned entities are already stored in the database. In case of dashboards, it will stop polling for changes in dashboard files and then restart it with new configurations after returning. If you are running Grafana Enterprise and have Fine-grained access control enabled, you need to have a permission with action \fBprovisioning:reload\fR and scope \fBprovisioners:dashboards\fR\&.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--describe-response-jsonschema\fP[=false]
	Print the JSON Schema of the response payload and exit without calling the API

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for admin-provisioning-reload-dashboards

.PP
\fB--raw\fP[=false]
	Print the raw HTTP response body instead of the decoded payload


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--api-key\fP=""
	API Key to authenticate to grafana server (env: GF_API_KEY)

.PP
\fB--base-path\fP="/api"
	Base path for server: useful when using sever behind reverse proxy (env: GF_BASE_PATH)

.PP
\fB--basic-user-password\fP=""
	Basic authentication password (env: GF_BASIC_AUTH_USERNAME)

.PP
\fB--basic-user-username\fP=""
	Basic authentication username (env: GF_BASIC_AUTH_PASSWORD)

.PP
\fB--debug\fP[=false]
	Enable debug logging (env: GF_DEBUG)

.PP
\fB--host\fP="localhost:3000"
	Grafana server host (env: GF_HOST)

.PP
\fB--org-id\fP=0
	Organization ID (env: GF_ORG_ID)


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBgf-admin-provisioning(1)\fP
